WEBVTT

00:00:04.719 --> 00:00:10.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday, first of May. Aisha Begum's absent today, so it's just us. Can everyone hear?</v>

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.250
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, bit tinny, but you're there.</v>

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:18.589
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Morning. The heating in the portakabin's apparently decided it's December.</v>

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.820
<v Jamie Brennan>You've still got your fleece on.</v>

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:29.079
<v Olumide Adeyemi>It's practically welded to me. Just an observation, before anyone gives me a thermostat to fix.</v>

00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:35.229
<v Callum Reid>We can hear the fan more than we can hear you.</v>

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:37.789
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Better now? Moved the microphone.</v>

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Much better, yeah.</v>

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:47.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the charity bake sale on Friday — today, obviously. I've been thinking it's Thursday all morning.</v>

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.049
<v Fiona Doyle>That's a dangerous mistake on a Friday.</v>

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:58.670
<v Jamie Brennan>Depends whether there's any cake left by the time stores get there.</v>

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:01.119
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not with this lot.</v>

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake allocation meeting. Updates first. Marcus?</v>

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.219
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'm here. Teams was hiding the unmute button from me.</v>

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:17.989
<v Marcus Hale>The purchase order chase — my deadline's moved. It's now by the 28th.</v>

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, got that.</v>

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.379
<v Marcus Hale>And, um, the other one isn't such good news.</v>

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:34.599
<v Marcus Hale>I can't get the training records for the new starters sorted because the parts haven't turned up. That's what's holding me up.</v>

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:36.870
<v Jamie Brennan>Ah, right.</v>

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:40.689
<v Marcus Hale>Bit frustrating, to be honest.</v>

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. Thanks. Controls next?</v>

00:01:44.739 --> 00:01:48.590
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, just finding my bit of paper. Very advanced system here.</v>

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:54.719
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I've greased and checked the bearings on the long belt. All done, no issues found.</v>

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.040
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nice when it's boring.</v>

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.340
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Boring's absolutely fine with me.</v>

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:03.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, anything to pass on before we get into today's stuff?</v>

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:10.889
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, passing this on for boss: the run to Kestrel for the replacement parts is done. All picked up.</v>

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:13.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers.</v>

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:15.969
<v Callum Reid>Am I next, or—</v>

00:02:16.599 --> 00:02:18.699
<v Fiona Doyle>Go on. Sorry, talked over you.</v>

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:21.870
<v Callum Reid>No, you're all right.</v>

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:32.120
<v Callum Reid>Booking a contractor to look at line two — I'm about halfway through that. Made some headway, but I haven't got the booking nailed down yet.</v>

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:33.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood.</v>

00:02:34.449 --> 00:02:39.699
<v Callum Reid>And I signed off the inspection on the 11kV board on Tuesday. That's already finished.</v>

00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:42.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Doyler?</v>

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:49.900
<v Fiona Doyle>The downtime for the Engel is all scheduled with production. That's sorted, no issues found with the arrangement.</v>

00:02:50.479 --> 00:02:51.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>That sounded remarkably painless.</v>

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.419
<v Fiona Doyle>Don't sound so surprised.</v>

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, today's new bits, then.</v>

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:05.900
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Arburg. Normal priority, and I'll have it done by the 28th.</v>

00:03:06.259 --> 00:03:08.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Doyler. Agreed on that.</v>

00:03:09.039 --> 00:03:10.240
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, okay.</v>

00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:14.770
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I've got one as well. Um— sorry, thought someone else was speaking.</v>

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:20.520
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'll write up the near miss at line 2 for next Tuesday. That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:25.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Olumide Adeyemi on the write-up, then.</v>

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:27.909
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.009
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, your audio clipped at the end there.</v>

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:37.639
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just said yep, that's mine. This microphone's having a morning.</v>

00:03:38.229 --> 00:03:46.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide Adeyemi, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the guard switch on two for Monday as well? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:54.699
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, sorry, I can't take that on for Monday. I haven't got the capacity to commit to it.</v>

00:03:56.289 --> 00:04:04.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Jamie, can you take the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the guard switch on two instead? Monday, and drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:06.439 --> 00:04:12.740
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take that. Lock-out tag-out sign-off on the guard switch on two, Monday. That gets first call.</v>

00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:14.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie.</v>

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:20.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>Glad you said no rather than just squeezing another thing in.</v>

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.680
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. Tempting to say yes when everyone's looking at you, isn't it.</v>

00:04:28.009 --> 00:04:32.560
<v Jamie Brennan>Half of us are looking at our own frozen faces, to be fair.</v>

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.970
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's the lot. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:38.290
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, all.</v>
